1078:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****         reception services:
1079:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback()
1080:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1081:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) In Non-Blocking mode transfers, possible errors are split into 2 categories.
1082:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****         Errors are handled as follows :
1083:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Error is considered as Recoverable and non blocking : Transfer could go till end, but er
1084:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            to be evaluated by user : this concerns Frame Error, Parity Error or Noise Error
1085:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            in Interrupt mode reception .
1086:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            Received character is then retrieved and stored in Rx buffer, Error code is set to allow
1087:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            to identify error type, and HAL_UART_ErrorCallback() user callback is executed.
1088:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            Transfer is kept ongoing on UART side.
1089:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            If user wants to abort it, Abort services should be called by user.
1090:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Error is considered as Blocking : Transfer could not be completed properly and is aborte
1091:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            This concerns Overrun Error In Interrupt mode reception and all errors in DMA mode.
1092:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            Error code is set to allow user to identify error type, and HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()
1093:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****            user callback is executed.
1094:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1095:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****     -@- In the Half duplex communication, it is forbidden to run the transmit
1096:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_uart.c ****         and receive process in parallel, the UART state HAL_UART_STATE_BUSY_TX_RX can't be useful.
